      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    int idx, size;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return '\\0';\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        long long x = 0;\n        for (; c >= '0' && c <= '9'; c = getChar()) {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        }\n        return static_cast<int>(sign * x);\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    // Allocate aligned prefix sum array: (n+1) rows of n columns\n    size_t total = static_cast<size_t>(n + 1) * n;\n    long long* prefRaw = nullptr;\n    if (posix_memalign(reinterpret_cast<void**>(&prefRaw), 64, sizeof(long long) * total) != 0) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n    // Zero first row\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) prefRaw[j] = 0;\n\n    // Read matrix and build vertical prefix sums with unrolled input reading\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        const size_t base = static_cast<size_t>(i) * n;\n        const size_t prev = static_cast<size_t>(i - 1) * n;\n        long long* __restrict curRow = prefRaw + base;\n        const long long* __restrict prevRow = prefRaw + prev;\n        int j = 0;\n        // Unrolled by 4\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            curRow[j]   = prevRow[j]   + v0;\n            curRow[j+1] = prevRow[j+1] + v1;\n            curRow[j+2] = prevRow[j+2] + v2;\n            curRow[j+3] = prevRow[j+3] + v3;\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            curRow[j] = prevRow[j] + v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long ans = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int limit = n - s;\n\n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:ans) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        const long long* __restrict top = prefRaw + static_cast<size_t>(i) * n;\n        const long long* __restrict bottom = prefRaw + static_cast<size_t>(i + s) * n;\n\n        // Initial window sum for columns [0, s-1]\n        long long window = 0;\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:window)\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n            window += bottom[j] - top[j];\n        }\n        long long curMax = window;\n\n        // Slide horizontally with unrolling by 4\n        int j = s;\n        const int end = n;\n        for (; j + 3 < end; j += 4) {\n            window += (bottom[j]   - top[j])   - (bottom[j-s]   - top[j-s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n            window += (bottom[j+1] - top[j+1]) - (bottom[j+1-s] - top[j+1-s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n            window += (bottom[j+2] - top[j+2]) - (bottom[j+2-s] - top[j+2-s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n            window += (bottom[j+3] - top[j+3]) - (bottom[j+3-s] - top[j+3-s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n        }\n        for (; j < end; ++j) {\n            window += (bottom[j] - top[j]) - (bottom[j-s] - top[j-s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n        }\n\n        if (curMax > ans) ans = curMax;\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", ans);\n    free(prefRaw);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating A's aligned allocation and __restrict qualifiers, B/C's buffered scanner and OpenMP parallel-for with SIMD reduction over rows, plus unrolling both input reading and the horizontal sliding-window scan reduces memory latency and loop overhead while preserving correctness across all sizes.",
  "notes": "The new solution combines: (1) FastScanner from B/C for low-overhead I/O; (2) vertical prefix sums built with an unrolled-by-4 read/compute loop; (3) posix_memalign to align the prefix array to 64 bytes, improving cache behavior and enabling better vectorization; (4) __restrict on row pointers to aid compiler optimizations; (5) OpenMP parallel-for over starting rows with static scheduling and a SIMD reduction for the initial window sum; (6) unrolled-by-4 horizontal sliding-window scan. All transformations are conservative and preserve exact output.",
